{"id":"U12","title":"The Power of Small Talk","titleZh":"闲聊的力量","paras":[{"id":"U12-P1","sentences":[{"id":"U12-P1-S1","hard":true,"text":"We've all been there: in a lift, in line at the bank or on an airplane, surrounded by people who are, like us, deeply focused on their smartphones or, worse, struggling with the uncomfortable silence."}],"zh":"我们都经历过这样的场景：在电梯里，在银行排队，或者在飞机上，周围都是和我们一样深深专注于智能手机的人，或者更糟糕的是，在令人不安的沉默中挣扎。"},{"id":"U12-P2","sentences":[{"id":"U12-P2-S1","hard":false,"text":"What's the problem?"},{"id":"U12-P2-S2","hard":false,"text":"It's possible that we all have compromised conversational intelligence."},{"id":"U12-P2-S3","hard":true,"text":"It's more likely that none of us start a conversation because it's awkward and challenging, or we think it's annoying and unnecessary."},{"id":"U12-P2-S4","hard":false,"text":"But the next time you find yourself among strangers, consider that small talk is worth the trouble."},{"id":"U12-P2-S5","hard":false,"text":"Experts say it's an invaluable social practice that results in big benefits."}],"zh":"问题出在哪里？有可能我们都存在受损的会话智能。更有可能的是，我们中没有人主动开启对话，因为这很尴尬且具有挑战性，或者我们认为这很烦人且没有必要。但下次当你发现自己身处陌生人之中时，请考虑一下闲聊是值得费这番功夫的。专家说这是一种宝贵的社交实践，能带来巨大的益处。"},{"id":"U12-P3","sentences":[{"id":"U12-P3-S1","hard":true,"text":"Dismissing small talk as unimportant is easy, but we can't forget that deep relationships wouldn't even exist if it weren't for casual conversation."},{"id":"U12-P3-S2","hard":false,"text":"Small talk is the grease for social communication, says Bernardo Carducci, director of the Shyness Research Institute at Indiana University Southeast."},{"id":"U12-P3-S3","hard":false,"text":"\"Almost every great love story and each big business deal begins with small talk,\" he explains."},{"id":"U12-P3-S4","hard":false,"text":"\"The key to successful small talk is learning how to connect with others, not just communicate with them.\""}],"zh":"把闲聊视为不重要而加以轻视很容易，但我们不能忘记，如果没有随意的交谈，深厚的关系甚至不会存在。印第安纳大学东南分校羞怯研究中心主任贝尔纳多·卡尔杜奇说，闲聊是社会沟通的润滑剂。\"几乎每一段伟大的爱情故事和每一笔大生意都是从闲聊开始的，\"他解释道。\"成功闲聊的关键是学会如何与他人建立联系，而不仅仅是与他们交流。\""},{"id":"U12-P4","sentences":[{"id":"U12-P4-S1","hard":false,"text":"In a 2014 study, Elizabeth Dunn, associate professor of psychology at UBC, invited people on their way into a coffee shop."},{"id":"U12-P4-S2","hard":false,"text":"One group was asked to seek out an interaction with its waiter; the other, to speak only when necessary."},{"id":"U12-P4-S3","hard":true,"text":"The results showed that those who chatted with their server reported significantly higher positive feelings and a better coffee shop experience."},{"id":"U12-P4-S4","hard":false,"text":"\"It's not that talking to the waiter is better than talking to your husband,\" says Dunn."},{"id":"U12-P4-S5","hard":false,"text":"\"But interactions with peripheral members of our social network matter for our well-being also.\""}],"zh":"在2014年的一项研究中，不列颠哥伦比亚大学心理学副教授伊丽莎白·邓恩邀请了正要进入咖啡店的人们。一组被要求主动与服务员进行互动；另一组则只在必要时才说话。结果显示，那些与服务员聊天的人报告了明显更高的积极情绪和更好的咖啡店体验。\"这并不是说与服务员交谈比与丈夫交谈更好，\"邓恩说。\"但与我们社交网络中的边缘成员的互动对我们的幸福感也很重要。\""},{"id":"U12-P5","sentences":[{"id":"U12-P5-S1","hard":true,"text":"Dunn believes that people who reach out to strangers feel a significantly greater sense of belonging, a bond with others."},{"id":"U12-P5-S2","hard":false,"text":"Carducci believes developing such a sense of belonging starts with small talk."},{"id":"U12-P5-S3","hard":false,"text":"\"Small talk is the basis of good manners,\" he says."}],"zh":"邓恩认为，主动接触陌生人的人会感受到明显更强的归属感，一种与他人的联结。卡尔杜奇认为，培养这种归属感始于闲聊。\"闲聊是良好礼仪的基础，\"他说。"}],"words":[{"id":"U12-W01","lemma":"lift","surface":"lift","pos":"n. / v.","zh":"n. 电梯; 搭便车 v. 举起; 提升","sent":"U12-P1-S1","phrases":[{"en":"in a lift","zh":"在电梯里"},{"en":"give sb. a lift","zh":"让某人搭便车"}]},{"id":"U12-W02","lemma":"in line","surface":"in line","pos":"phr.","zh":"排队; 成一直线","sent":"U12-P1-S1","phrases":[{"en":"wait in line","zh":"排队等候"}]},{"id":"U12-W03","lemma":"surround","surface":"surrounded","pos":"v.","zh":"围绕; 包围","sent":"U12-P1-S1","phrases":[{"en":"be surrounded by","zh":"被...包围"}]},{"id":"U12-W04","lemma":"deeply","surface":"deeply","pos":"adv.","zh":"深深地; 非常","sent":"U12-P1-S1","phrases":[{"en":"deeply focused","zh":"深深专注于"}]},{"id":"U12-W05","lemma":"focus on","surface":"focused on","pos":"phr. v.","zh":"专注于; 集中于","sent":"U12-P1-S1","phrases":[{"en":"be focused on","zh":"专注于..."}]},{"id":"U12-W06","lemma":"smartphone","surface":"smartphones","pos":"n.","zh":"智能手机","sent":"U12-P1-S1","phrases":[{"en":"use smartphones","zh":"使用智能手机"}]},{"id":"U12-W07","lemma":"struggle","surface":"struggling","pos":"v.","zh":"挣扎; 努力; 斗争","sent":"U12-P1-S1","phrases":[{"en":"struggle with","zh":"与...挣扎"},{"en":"struggle for","zh":"为...奋斗"}]},{"id":"U12-W08","lemma":"uncomfortable","surface":"uncomfortable","pos":"adj.","zh":"不舒服的; 令人不安的","sent":"U12-P1-S1","phrases":[{"en":"uncomfortable silence","zh":"令人不安的沉默"}]},{"id":"U12-W09","lemma":"silence","surface":"silence","pos":"n. / v.","zh":"n. 沉默; 寂静 v. 使安静","sent":"U12-P1-S1","phrases":[{"en":"in silence","zh":"沉默地"},{"en":"break the silence","zh":"打破沉默"}]},{"id":"U12-W10","lemma":"compromise","surface":"compromised","pos":"v. / adj.","zh":"v. 妥协; 损害 adj. 受损的; 妥协的","sent":"U12-P2-S2","phrases":[{"en":"compromised intelligence","zh":"受损的智力"}]},{"id":"U12-W11","lemma":"conversational","surface":"conversational","pos":"adj.","zh":"会话的; 交谈的","sent":"U12-P2-S2","phrases":[{"en":"conversational intelligence","zh":"会话智能"}]},{"id":"U12-W12","lemma":"intelligence","surface":"intelligence","pos":"n.","zh":"智力; 智能; 情报","sent":"U12-P2-S2","phrases":[{"en":"artificial intelligence","zh":"人工智能"},{"en":"emotional intelligence","zh":"情商"}]},{"id":"U12-W13","lemma":"conversation","surface":"conversation","pos":"n.","zh":"对话; 交谈","sent":"U12-P2-S2","phrases":[{"en":"start a conversation","zh":"开启对话"},{"en":"have a conversation","zh":"进行对话"}]},{"id":"U12-W14","lemma":"awkward","surface":"awkward","pos":"adj.","zh":"尴尬的; 笨拙的","sent":"U12-P2-S3","phrases":[{"en":"awkward silence","zh":"尴尬